deeper.body:
Typical detection bookkeeping you will meet in the following pages (beyond this page, but previewed by p.357 and p.360):

- converting COCO's `x, y, width, height` pixel boxes into normalized coordinates;
- assigning each ground-truth box to a grid cell;
- building target tensors for boxes, confidences and classes;
- decoding model outputs back into boxes and filtering by confidence.

None of this is deep math; it is indexing and geometry that must be exactly right.
